Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 11:47:12 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Absolute knockback profiles

A profile with absolute: true sets the victim's velocity on a player melee hit (horizontal along the
attacker-to-victim line, vertical up) instead of adding to its motion; friction, the add values and the
vertical limits are skipped, the (wtap-)extra values still apply. client-sprint: true also counts the
client's sprint packets as sprinting, so stop-sprint no longer drops the sprint extra while W is held.
Adds the 'absolute' preset (the practice plugin's AbsoluteKnockback values).

diff --git a/src/main/java/dev/cobblesword/nachospigot/knockback/KnockbackProfile.java b/src/main/java/dev/cobblesword/nachospigot/knockback/KnockbackProfile.java
index dff10378..25b70b38 100644
--- a/src/main/java/dev/cobblesword/nachospigot/knockback/KnockbackProfile.java
+++ b/src/main/java/dev/cobblesword/nachospigot/knockback/KnockbackProfile.java
@@ -102,6 +102,26 @@ public interface KnockbackProfile {
 	
 	void setAddVertical(double addVertical);
 
+	/**
+	 * Absolute knockback: a player melee hit replaces the victim's velocity with
+	 * {@code horizontal} along the attacker-to-victim line and {@code vertical}, instead of
+	 * adding them to the victim's own motion. Friction, the vertical limits and the add
+	 * values are not used for that hit; the (wtap-)extra values are still added on top.
+	 * Projectiles keep the normal formula.
+	 */
+	boolean isAbsolute();
+
+	void setAbsolute(boolean absolute);
+
+	/**
+	 * Also count the attacker as sprinting while its client says so (start/stop sprint
+	 * packets), not only while the server flag is set. Stop-sprint clears only the server
+	 * flag, so with this on every hit while W is held gets the wtap-extra values.
+	 */
+	boolean isClientSprint();
+
+	void setClientSprint(boolean clientSprint);
+
 	String[] getKnockbackValues();
 
 	String[] getProjectilesValues();
